Name languages without the GNU locale identification category.

lightdm_language_get_name() and lightdm_language_get_territory() look a
language's English name up through LC_IDENTIFICATION and
nl_langinfo(_NL_IDENTIFICATION_LANGUAGE/_TERRITORY), a GNU C library
extension, after finding an installed locale with "locale -a".  Where the
C library has no such category (LikeOS's has one built-in locale and no
locale program) the build stopped on the undeclared names.  The lookup is
now compiled only where the category exists; elsewhere both functions use
the fallback they already had -- the language and territory codes.

